# Trivy ignore list
#
# Scope: applies to `make image-scan` (OCI image scanning) and `make trivy-fs`
# (filesystem scanning). trivy picks this file up automatically from the
# working directory.
#
# Suppression policy:
#   - Every entry requires a CVE ID, a one-line reason, and an upstream tracker.
#   - Re-evaluate the list after every Paketo buildpack / base-image refresh.
#     If the CVE drops off a new image scan, remove the entry.
#
# ------------------------------------------------------------
# Paketo buildpack helper binaries — Go stdlib 1.26.1
# ------------------------------------------------------------
# These CVEs live in tiny Go helpers baked into every spring-boot:build-image
# output:
#     /layers/paketo-buildpacks_ca-certificates/helper/helper
#     /layers/paketo-buildpacks_spring-boot/helper/helper
# They run ONCE at container start (symlink setup + JVM launcher) and are not
# reachable from application request paths. Fix is exclusively upstream:
# Paketo must rebuild their buildpacks against Go 1.26.2+. Once they do, the
# next `mvn spring-boot:build-image` will pull a refreshed layer and these
# entries become dead code — remove them.
#
# Upstream tracker: https://github.com/paketo-buildpacks/spring-boot/issues
#                   https://github.com/paketo-buildpacks/ca-certificates/issues
CVE-2026-32280
CVE-2026-32281
CVE-2026-32282
CVE-2026-32283
CVE-2026-33810

# ------------------------------------------------------------
# Paketo / CNB Go binaries — Go stdlib 1.26.4 (disclosed 2026-07)
# ------------------------------------------------------------
# CVE-2026-39822 (HIGH, os.Root symlink following; fixed in Go 1.26.5 / 1.25.12)
# hits SIX gobinary targets in every spring-boot:build-image output, all compiled
# by upstream with Go 1.26.4:
#     /cnb/lifecycle/launcher
#     /layers/paketo-buildpacks_bellsoft-liberica/helper/helper
#     /layers/paketo-buildpacks_ca-certificates/helper/helper
#     /layers/paketo-buildpacks_spring-boot/helper/helper
#     (+ the two lifecycle launcher SBOM documents that describe them)
# Same reachability profile as the 1.26.1 block above: these run ONCE at container
# start (JVM launch + symlink/CA setup) and are not reachable from any application
# request path; none of them walks an untrusted filesystem tree via os.Root.
# The fix is exclusively upstream — Paketo/CNB must rebuild against Go 1.26.5+.
#
# TIME-BOXED: `exp:` makes trivy re-arm the gate on this date so the waiver cannot
# quietly become permanent. On expiry, re-run `make image-scan`: if Paketo has
# shipped a refreshed builder the CVE is simply gone and this block should be
# deleted; if not, re-date it with a fresh check of the trackers below.
#
# Upstream tracker: https://github.com/buildpacks/lifecycle/releases
#                   https://github.com/paketo-buildpacks/spring-boot/issues
#                   https://github.com/paketo-buildpacks/ca-certificates/issues
CVE-2026-39822 exp:2026-08-17
